# MediFlow project rules (Cursor)

Cursor reads **`AGENTS.md`** natively, and that file is this repo's single entry point for every
coding agent. This rule exists only to make the pointer explicit — it deliberately contains **no
rules of its own**, so there is nothing here to drift out of sync.

## ⚡ First thing every session

Before writing ANY code, read the changelog:
```bash
node scripts/changelog.js --summary
node scripts/changelog.js --limit 5
```

## Where the instructions are

1. **[`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md)** at the repo root — project overview, read order, hard rules.
2. **[`docs/ai/`](../../docs/ai/README.md)** — the actual standards, in full. This is the source of truth.
3. **[`frontend/AGENTS.md`](../../frontend/AGENTS.md)** — takes precedence inside `frontend/`
   (the AGENTS.md spec says the nearest file wins).

## The one thing worth repeating

The Java standards (clean architecture, JPA, `@PreAuthorize`, `BigDecimal`) govern the `*-service/`
modules **only**. Inside `frontend/`, follow `docs/ai/12-frontend.md` instead — do not build
`domain/application/infrastructure` trees in TypeScript.
